        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >ZENVADER is a bullet-hell roguelite shooter inspired by classic shooting games in the 80s.<br><br> You pilot a “Battle Unit”, the last hope for mankind, and take on an army of powerful aliens.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Four Battle Units</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are four types of battle units that you can pilot: a unit that excels in rapid fire, a unit that excels in penetrating ability and destructive power, a unit that fights using indirect means such as wall shot and missiles, and so on. Each unit has its own characteristics and requires different strategies.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Take Orbs to Power Up</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your unit is weak at first, but by taking orbs dropped by the aliens, you can temporarily enhance its rapid-firing speed, movement speed, damage dealt, and so on.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Unlock New Weapons at Space Hangar</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >By spending “Alien Materia” acquired by defeating aliens, you can unlock new weapons and permanently increase various parameters. The more you fight, the stronger you become, and eventually you will be able to defeat the foes that you thought you could never defeat.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Challenge yourself to Speedrun</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Once your units are fully upgraded, try beating the campaign mode as fast as possible. While the typical clear time is around 20-25 minutes, optimizing your movements and refining your tactics can make clearing it under 15 minutes is not entirely impossible. So, how fast can you get? </p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >ZENVADER is a bullet-hell roguelite shooter inspired by classic shooting games in the 80s.<br><br> You pilot a “Battle Unit”, the last hope for mankind, and take on an army of powerful aliens.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Four Battle Units</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are four types of battle units that you can pilot: a unit that excels in rapid fire, a unit that excels in penetrating ability and destructive power, a unit that fights using indirect means such as wall shot and missiles, and so on. Each unit has its own characteristics and requires different strategies.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Take Orbs to Power Up</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your unit is weak at first, but by taking orbs dropped by the aliens, you can temporarily enhance its rapid-firing speed, movement speed, damage dealt, and so on.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Unlock New Weapons at Space Hangar</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >By spending “Alien Materia” acquired by defeating aliens, you can unlock new weapons and permanently increase various parameters. The more you fight, the stronger you become, and eventually you will be able to defeat the foes that you thought you could never defeat.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Challenge yourself to Speedrun</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Once your units are fully upgraded, try beating the campaign mode as fast as possible. While the typical clear time is around 20-25 minutes, optimizing your movements and refining your tactics can make clearing it under 15 minutes is not entirely impossible. So, how fast can you get? </p>",
        "short_description": "Zenvader is a super retro shooter mixed with roguelite elements. Dodge the barrage of bullets, improve your unit, and try to defeat the Alien King!",
        "supported_languages": "English, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese",
        "reviews": "“When I first started playing, I thought, “Ah I see, I guess this is another those-type (roguelite-surviver) of game,” and didn’t take it too seriously. But when I realized I’d been playing nonstop for seven hours, I came to the conclusion that it’s definitely more than just that. (Weekly Famitsu, April 23, 2026 issue)”<br>週刊ファミ通　2026年4月23日号<br><br>“A battle that determines the fate of humanity, reviving the spirit of the '80s”<br>Indie Freaks <br>",
